  "mach:governance": "academic",
  "mach:foundation": "Division of Medical Image Computing, DKFZ",
  "mach:category": "medical-imaging-signals",
  "mach:subcategory": "imaging-model",
  "mach:maturity": "beta",
  "mach:judgement": "Assess",
  "mach:judgementReason": "Applies nnU-Net's self-configuring philosophy to 3D detection, filling a genuine gap — detection benchmarks in medical imaging are far less standardised than segmentation. MICCAI 2021 paper, 630 stars, Apache-2.0. However, it has seen less community adoption than nnU-Net and the version has not progressed beyond 0.1. Worth tracking closely, especially for lung nodule and lesion detection pipelines.",
  "mach:editorialReviewedAt": "2026-05-11",
